@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

<p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> April 9, 2026</p>

<p>At <strong>Amethyst</strong>, your privacy matters to us. We designed Amethyst to help students stay organized, manage study sessions, track productivity, and build healthier academic habits in a way that feels supportive and personal. This Privacy Policy explains what information Amethyst may collect, how it may be used, and how we aim to protect your data while you use the platform.</p>

<h2>Information We May Collect</h2>
<p>Amethyst may collect information that you choose to provide while using the platform, including account details, profile information, study session entries, course-related information, task and productivity data, notes, and other content you create within the app. If certain features are available, Amethyst may also store preferences related to timers, study routines, or personalized productivity settings.</p>

<p>We may also collect basic technical information such as browser type, device type, access times, and general usage activity to help improve performance and user experience.</p>

<h2>How Your Information May Be Used</h2>
<p>The information stored in Amethyst may be used to support core platform features, such as displaying your study sessions, organizing your coursework, tracking progress, saving notes, and personalizing your experience. We may also use information to improve site functionality, troubleshoot technical issues, monitor performance, and better understand how students interact with the platform.</p>

<p>Amethyst is intended to make productivity feel more manageable, so data may also be used to present helpful reminders, session summaries, or feature suggestions based on your activity within the app.</p>

<h2>Personalization and Productivity Features</h2>
<p>Some Amethyst features are designed to provide a more personalized experience. This may include displaying your planned and completed study sessions, productivity notes, timer settings, focus tools, or other study-related information connected to your account. These features are meant to help support your routines and are only visible within your own experience unless otherwise stated.</p>

<h2>Data Sharing</h2>
<p>Amethyst does not sell your personal information. Information entered into the platform is intended to remain within the application experience and be used only for platform-related purposes. In limited situations, information may be accessed by authorized administrators, developers, or support personnel for maintenance, troubleshooting, testing, or security purposes.</p>

<h2>Data Storage and Security</h2>
<p>We aim to store information securely and take reasonable steps to protect user data from unauthorized access, misuse, or disclosure. While no system can guarantee complete security, Amethyst is built with the intention of handling student information responsibly and thoughtfully.</p>

<p>Users are encouraged to keep their login credentials secure and avoid sharing their account access with others.</p>

<h2>User Content</h2>
<p>Any notes, study session details, productivity entries, or other content you enter into Amethyst remain your responsibility. Please avoid storing highly sensitive personal information in free-response fields unless the platform specifically requests it for a feature.</p>

<h2>Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
<p>Amethyst may use cookies or similar technologies to support login sessions, remember preferences, and improve the overall functionality of the platform. These tools help create a smoother and more personalized experience while using the site.</p>

<h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
<p>If Amethyst integrates with third-party tools, services, or APIs, some information may be processed through those services in order for certain features to function. These services may have their own privacy policies and data practices. Amethyst aims to use third-party tools thoughtfully and only where helpful to the user experience.</p>

<h2>Your Choices</h2>
<p>You may be able to review, update, or remove certain information connected to your account through the platform. You may also choose what kinds of notes, study details, or profile content you add to the app. Because Amethyst is designed to support student organization, you remain in control of the content you enter.</p>

<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>Amethyst may update this Privacy Policy from time to time as the platform grows and changes. Any updates will be reflected on this page with a revised effective date. Continued use of the platform after updates means you accept the revised policy.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how information is handled within Amethyst, please contact the Amethyst team through the appropriate support or project contact channel.</p>